<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yashovarman of Kannauj</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yashovarman was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the early 8th century, who restored the city's power after the collapse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>'s empire. He patronised the playwright <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhavabhuti">Bhavabhuti</a> and the poet Vakpatiraja, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a> epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaudavaho">Gaudavaho</a> celebrates his campaigns, but he was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida">Lalitaditya Muktapida</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>.</p></div>
